  "reason": "The assistant contradicts key factual claims from the reference regarding the maximum early retirement period (claiming five years instead of two) and the partial pension starting age (claiming 63 instead of the official retirement age). These are significant factual errors that misinform the user about the actual legal provisions.",
  "evidence": "The assistant states: \"The maximum early retirement age was raised from two years to five years before the official retirement age\" and \"You can now retire earlier, later, or at the official age. Early retirement (Taking the pension earlier): From when: You can now retire up to five years earlier than the official retirement age.\" Additionally, it states: \"You can also draw a partial pension (typically 20%, 40%, or 60% of the full pension) starting from the official retirement age (currently 65 for men, 64 for women)\" which contradicts the reference stating partial pension can be drawn \"from 63\"."
